'''''Phyllarthron bojerianum''''' is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Bignoniaceae]].<ref name = powo/> It is a shrub or tree endemic to [[Madagascar]] that grows 10 to 15 meters tall. It is widespread on the island, where it grows in [[Madagascar lowland forests|humid lowland and littoral forests]], [[Madagascar dry deciduous forests|dry deciduous forests]], and [[Madagascar subhumid forests|lowland and montane subhumid forests]] from 5 to 2180 meters elevation.<ref name = iucn/>

The species was first described by [[Augustin Pyramus de Candolle]] in 1845.<ref name = iucn/>

